<Section
  id="insight"
  label="Insight"
  title="The address is computed from the record"
  lede="A database finds a record by walking an index, a catalogue that grows with every entry. This engine computes the address from the record itself, so there is no index to size, store, or repair."
>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      Two systems that observe the same thing arrive at the same address without talking to each
      other, so a record can be checked by recomputing its address, without trusting the system
      that wrote it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Time is one of the axes, so a time window is answered from the same structure as every other
      question. The memory an answer costs does not grow with the number of records, which is what
      lets the engine run inside the memory a small part carries.
    </p>
  </div>
</Section>
